      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T08:30:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "_apply_bootmode duplicates _ensure_bootmode. By the time _apply_bootmode_with_retry (399) calls it, _ensure_bootmode has already read current (412), read pending and resolved conflicts (417-439), and returned early on desired\u003d\u003dcurrent (441), so this method\u0027s current read (481), pending-conflict abort (486-496) and skip (497) are unreachable in production (_apply_bootmode has no caller but _apply_bootmode_with_retry, which has none but _ensure_bootmode). Folding the set into _apply_bootmode_with_retry drops ~35 dead lines and 2-4 redundant BMC reads, behavior-identical:\n\n    attrs \u003d {\"BootMode\": host_obj.bootmode}\n    if await self.hardware_dispatcher.set_bios_attribute(attrs):\n        return True\n    if not await self._clear_bootmode_jobs(host_obj):\n        return False\n    return await self.hardware_dispatcher.set_bios_attribute(attrs)\n\nThe direct _apply_bootmode unit tests then fold away (covered end-to-end in TestPrepareHostHardwareBootmode). Minor: _read_bootmode (374) and _pending_bootmode (384) take a host_obj they never use.",
      "revId": "312048961173ffb5fdd481dbeca832bd6fa792c0",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
