      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T11:03:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Addressed in patch set 10: _apply_bootmode is folded into _apply_bootmode_with_retry exactly as suggested (set, clear once on failure, set again), the \"does not match desired, setting it\" warning moved up into _ensure_bootmode where current and desired are both in scope, and the direct unit tests folded away. standard.py is 27 lines net smaller and the duplicate BMC reads are gone. _read_bootmode() and _pending_bootmode() no longer take the unused host_obj.\n\nOne wording note, because the distinction matters for how we triage this kind of finding: those branches were redundant, not dead. Dead code is unreachable by construction; these were reachable, just duplicated. _apply_bootmode\u0027s own current-read could still return None if the BMC failed transiently between it and the read _ensure_bootmode had just done, and on the post-clear retry the pending re-read could legitimately observe a different value. What makes the fold safe is not that the branches could never execute, it is that _ensure_bootmode already performs both checks immediately beforehand and Badfish.set_bios_attribute() skips the PATCH when the applied value already matches, so removing the second weaker copy loses no behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "b4cbd4b5_27a1824a",
      "revId": "312048961173ffb5fdd481dbeca832bd6fa792c0",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
